      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is implementation guidance, and does not belong in the top description. I recommend this:\n\n[PROPOSED]\n\nSystem resources are defined by the default component store. They represent any physical or abstract entities of limited availability that is required for a component instance to execute and process work.\n\nEach defined resource has an id. The use of a resource is specified by the amount\nand the kind (e.g. whether the amount of resources is required for each frame processed, or whether they are required regardless of the processing rate (const amount)).\n\nNote: implementations can shadow this structure with their own custom resource structure where a uint32_t based enum is used for id. This can be used to provide\na name for each resource, via parameter descriptors.",
